    "q-161060": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161060",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n⟨\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,,\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,,\\,\\text{_______}⟩\n$$\n\n \n\nThe fundamental vector product of the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=\\sqrt{z-1}$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis for $z\\in [1,10]$ is given above. What is the $3$rd component of the product?",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $y=\\sqrt{z-1}\\ge 0$ for all $z\\in [1,10].$ The parametrization of our surface of revolution is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,f(z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,(z,\\theta )\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(z)=\\sqrt{z-1},$ and  \n\n$$\nD=\\{(z,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le 10,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂z}⟩=⟨{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta }⟩=⟨f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-{f}^{′}f{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -{f}^{′}f{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-{f}^{′}f⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f=\\sqrt{z-1},$ we obtain ${f}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z-1}}.$ So, finally, we conclude that the fundamental vector product is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}=⟨\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
